DataFlint (https://github.com/dataflint/spark), tag v0.9.9
(commit 27b995bba2027c3001765642ac662ffe2174af72). It ships no NOTICE file.
The remediation text of these rules adapts the suggestions in these files
under spark-ui/src/reducers/Alerts/:

  plan.smj-small-side           JoinToBroadcastAlert.ts
  plan.broadcast-too-large      BroadcastTooLargeAlert.ts
  plan.cartesian                LargeCrossJoinScanAlert.ts
  plan.long-filter              LongFilterConditions.ts
  plan.small-files-read         MemorySQLInputOutputAlerts.ts
  plan.small-files-written      MemorySQLInputOutputAlerts.ts
  stage.oversized-partitions    MaxPartitionToBigAlert.ts
  stage.tiny-tasks              SmallTasksAlert.ts
  executor.idle-cores           WastedCoresAlertsReducer.ts
  executor.memory-under         MemoryAlertsReducer.ts
  executor.memory-over          MemoryAlertsReducer.ts
  executor.driver-memory-under  MemoryAlertsReducer.ts

The way plan.smj-small-side sizes each join side, through the chain of
operators above it, follows spark-ui/src/reducers/PlanGraphUtils.ts.

SparkDoctor (https://github.com/khodosko/sparkDoctor), tag v0.1.5.
Copyright 2026 SparkDoctor contributors. It ships no NOTICE file. The lessons
of these rules adapt the detection criteria described in docs/detections.md:
plan.many-exchanges, plan.repeated-subtree, plan.missed-exchange-reuse,
stage.task-skew, stage.shuffle-skew, stage.oversized-partitions,
stage.low-shuffle-parallelism, stage.tiny-tasks, stage.spill,
stage.spill-skew, stage.executor-imbalance, stage.host-imbalance,
stage.retry-waste and stage.speculation.

Dr. Elephant (https://github.com/linkedin/dr-elephant), commit
916c25d5845f534ec2648fe17d978cd48a8bd284. Copyright 2016 LinkedIn Corp. The
lessons of stage.gc-pressure and executor.memory-over adapt how
app/com/linkedin/drelephant/spark/heuristics/ExecutorGcHeuristic.scala reads
its GC ratio: high as too little executor memory, and low as more than the
tasks need.
